  "equipment_type": "Energy recovery ventilation unit controller",
  "applies_to": "Nuaire XBOXER XBC supply and extract heat recovery units, sizes 10-65, with the EcoSmart Connect (CO) FAC controller.",
  "summary": "The FAC controller in Nuaire XBOXER XBC units (EcoSmart Connect CO) is a BACnet MS/TP device; a BACnet IP router (ESCO-IPN) is offered for IP networks. The manual's list by instance number has 166 objects in the 10005-18258 range: temperatures and room module values (AI), fan and heating outputs, relay states, setpoints and fan settings (AV), enables, modes and alarms (MSV), six schedules and a calendar. Nuaire's BPS and Boxer BPS manuals (671828, 671873) use mostly the same instances.",
  "bacnet_transport": [
    "BACnet MS/TP"
  ],
  "firmware": "Strategy SW-FAC2612-2-12A (per object 17340)",
  "default_device_instance": null,
  "access_inferred": true,
  "notes": [
    "The list has no read/write column. Access here is inferred: inputs and outputs are R, objects with a default value are W, and status, room module and alarm values are R.",
    "Many 'Ala (...)' and 'Norm (...)' MSVs exist only to raise LCD events; use the main alarm MSVs (Critical Alarm, Maint. Alarm, Frost Alarm, supply temperature alarms) instead.",
    "RM199-RM203 and RM212-RM215 are room modules on the controller's sensor bus; their objects carry values only when that module is fitted.",
    "CAL 10496 Local Calendar and SCH 10496 Time Schedule share instance 10496 (different object types). The Setpoint Schedule AV is printed as 18215- and listed as 18215.",
    "The same manual also has a by-category list. Nuaire's BPS H-CO (671828) and Boxer BPS (671873) manuals use mostly the same 10xxx instances, but some names differ and 671828 lacks the RM occupancy and test objects; check the unit's own manual. Nuaire's later EcoSmart Connect manuals (672040, 672059) use a 28xxx range."
  ],
  "source": {
    "title": "XBOXER XBC unit sizes 10-65 with EcoSmart Connect (CO) control - Installation and Maintenance, 12.1 BACnet Object List (By Instance Number)",
    "doc_number": "671748",
    "revision_date": "2020-11-25",
    "url": "https://info.nuaire.co.uk/IandM/671748.pdf"
  },
  "integration": {
    "summary": "Set MV 10218 Enable to On (2) to run the unit, then write AV 17761 Fan Speed Demand (0 % = trickle) and AV 10309 Software Setpoint. Read the supply, fresh and extract air temperatures, BO 10191 Fan Enabled Cmd and the alarm MSVs; BV 10332 resets latched alarms. Variables are normally written at priority 16.",
    "minimum_points": [
      {
        "ref": "MV 10218",
        "name": "Enable",
        "why": "Software enable (1 = Off, 2 = On)"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AV 17761",
        "name": "Fan Speed Demand",
        "why": "Fan speed demand, % (0 % = trickle)"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AV 10309",
        "name": "Software Setpoint",
        "why": "Temperature setpoint, °C"
      },
      {
        "ref": "BV 10332",
        "name": "Reset Alarms",
        "why": "Reset latched alarms"
      },
      {
        "ref": "BO 10191",
        "name": "Fan Enabled Cmd",
        "why": "Fan enable relay state"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 10005",
        "name": "Supply Air Temp (B)",
        "why": "Supply air temperature"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 10008",
        "name": "Fresh Air Temp (H)",
        "why": "Fresh (outdoor) air temperature"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 10011",
        "name": "Extract Air Temp (C)",
        "why": "Extract air temperature"
      },
      {
        "ref": "BO 10188",
        "name": "Fault Relay Cmd",
        "why": "Fault relay (0 = Alarm, 1 = Normal)"
      },
      {
        "ref": "MV 15309",
        "name": "Critical Alarm",
        "why": "Latched critical alarm (2 = Alarm)"
      }
    ],
    "enable": "The unit runs from the software Enable MSV, the switched-live enable input (IN8), the schedule, night cooling, purge, or room module PIR and fan override inputs. MV 10214 SetPoint Op decides whether the software setpoint or the last changed setpoint is used.",
    "heartbeat": null,
    "remote_sensors": "AV 17773 BMS 0-10v Input is a virtual 0-10 V input for ESClassic BMS mode (MV 17608 OUT4 Mode). AV 17971 sets how long a changed setpoint holds before reverting when 'last changed with timeout' is selected.",
    "setup": [
      "BACnet MS/TP on the FC bus; the MAC address is set on the FAC controller's DIP switch.",
      "An ESCO-IPN BACnet IP to MS/TP router is available for IP networks."
    ],
    "gotchas": [
      "AV, BV and MSV values are written at priority 16 and stay; outputs (AO, BO) are driven by the strategy at 16, so manual overrides use priority 8 and must be relinquished.",
      "AI and BI objects are read-only.",
      "Test (...) MSVs are factory-use only."
    ]
  },
